   "Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}}]], "Text", \
"BlockQuote",
 Background->None,ExpressionUUID->"0b602246-3b9a-304e-9906-0e4fb19afb69"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["5.2. Hidden assumption 2: negligible interface geometry", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"ab8626c0-481d-cf40-95c0-2ca84dcd1bd6"],

Cell["\<\
In practice, interface geometry is often treated as calibration detail rather \
than ontological input.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a5648432-e9b5-5b46-8c27-5a374ec5de21"],

Cell["\<\
But if closure and phase-locking matter, then geometry may determine which \
modes become visible. \
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b740aa02-011d-7545-b857-e04bebec0431"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["5.3. Hidden assumption 3: transduction neutrality", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"6ae67c38-d81b-1b4a-985d-43925ebf1c8d"],

Cell["A detector is often treated as a neutral reporter.", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"12b7320f-f788-2444-9984-e7818a97bb0d"],

Cell["\<\
In reality it is a selective dynamical system with its own resonance \
structure, memory, thresholds, and nonlinearities. \
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c7adc520-9edc-9945-9533-3c3a96914b4f"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["5.4. Hidden assumption 4: value primacy", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"87c369fc-f05b-2b4e-b4cf-506f8f55b894"],

Cell["\<\
Science often privileges the final reported value over the full structure of \
the measuring event.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"92c1a130-ba3e-b042-9dbd-fc20a71006bc"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "RHUFT instead proposes ",
 StyleBox["measurement state reporting",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 ", not just scalar reporting. "
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"721e4459-c969-a947-be81-dd8dd069f75d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[GridBox[{
