Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["10. Interface geometry as a first-class scientific variable", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"d3187936-d9c8-5944-8490-6ec7f9b9650b"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["10.1. Why geometry matters", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"1734c9f4-5969-b843-a856-fc22427e5fa5"],

Cell["\<\
If the field has structured node distributions or preferred stabilization \
pathways, then interface geometry influences what the instrument can couple \
to. \
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a750b9f0-266d-3c42-bc77-a5a35eaea7a5"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["10.2. Examples of geometry-sensitive measurement", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"5a369436-f250-fa49-811f-a28366b2dd08"],

Cell["antenna arrays,", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"72d104b1-99b1-094f-beed-5f5e217be4a8"],

Cell["optical cavity shapes,", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"d4a85b1b-ab9d-e74b-9ce3-1c46b8fec24c"],

Cell["sensor lattice topology,", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"188558e1-938e-e245-9bd5-f2c1bd3e4ec5"],

Cell["metamaterial detector surfaces,", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"ed189672-1690-3543-91f2-216e700779a6"],

Cell["resonant electrode arrangements,", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"3a3378be-bbd3-4840-868a-55b593a696ef"],

Cell["spherical or toroidal pickup geometries.", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"a5f4d699-5ee0-6f40-ab45-3c5a4c82e94e"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["10.3. RHUFT design principle", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"d7c6002c-c2e7-e841-a452-1e1eaa01e039"],

Cell["\<\
Instrument geometry should not only be optimized for signal intensity, but \
also for: \
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7b0f6916-656d-234e-99f6-ef8956e493aa"],

Cell["closure sensitivity,", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"20a7b598-9478-a54c-a765-c32c6a6da755"],

Cell["phase selectivity,", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"832c609b-07d4-b849-a979-b29c2b4a3ad3"],

Cell["multiscale coupling,", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"477696e8-f36c-094b-9c7a-f3a1765a6bda"],

Cell["recurrence support,", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"7604a93f-3d76-354f-a83f-946c6a937c96"],

Cell["topological mode discrimination.", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"1188a85a-a297-0340-8612-371d55fa59bc"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["10.4. Practical breakthrough path", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"660e527c-21ab-1c4e-9a7f-d2794b7b821d"],

Cell["\<\
This is realistic. One can prototype geometry-sensitive sensor arrays and \
compare readout structures across: \
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c09c5f66-dd55-1a49-99d9-de68f461b0ff"],

Cell["planar arrangements,", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"70c2b6cb-222b-f446-b939-1f1ec245ef2f"],

Cell["Fibonacci/golden-angle arrays,", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"71ae910e-1063-4e44-8e00-a2641da44fd8"],

Cell["toroidal loop systems,", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"1707bafb-69a4-8144-8735-bd54ca35d32a"],

Cell["quasi-periodic lattices.", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"f07f713e-58ef-904d-bdb7-5ed0a1706e6c"],

Cell["This is a direct experimental path. ", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"24054cfd-7f95-c841-9559-677542376dda"],

