    "Columns" -> {False, {True}, False}, "Rows" -> {False, {True}, False}},
   GridBoxItemSize->{"Columns" -> {{Fit}}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}}],
  "Grid"]], "Text", "MarkdownDelimiter",
 ShowStringCharacters->False,
 Background->None,ExpressionUUID->"d5f27292-9c81-1348-b60f-c17ddc3d284b"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["14. Realistically approachable breakthroughs", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"5dffaf5d-b0f0-df41-beea-4e6d60682bcd"],

Cell["This section is intentionally practical. ", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"573ee69b-dd21-6246-86c3-ebc7a4fbfce4"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["14.1. Breakthrough class A: geometry-differential sensing", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"d67e0ecb-19da-484e-a327-456628f8f0b2"],

Cell["\<\
Build otherwise equivalent sensors that differ only by interface geometry: \
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"42acca34-4ff8-ca43-b7ee-33a2b0d13feb"],

Cell["linear array,", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"4de37cf3-2e33-7d4c-97dc-2f3d6a9dbec8"],

Cell["circular array,", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"531042f0-5234-4344-81d6-f477de03f8cd"],

Cell["Fibonacci spiral,", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"ddc69b11-1ad3-7f49-973e-b6efc63ec052"],

Cell["toroidal loop,", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"484d6929-133a-8549-8967-e90a9b829257"],

Cell["quasi-periodic surface.", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"be2198c3-4561-4b45-b8b7-1d2bb4b288d6"],

Cell["Test whether: ", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"02c79946-4829-c54d-b456-ab6ad999cb10"],

Cell["noise structure differs,", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"4e7ca0ff-fdb5-a443-bb52-1e5d40bddb61"],

Cell["weak-signal pickup differs,", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"5fb3746f-d9ae-474c-8da1-4c61cfe62168"],

Cell["phase sensitivity differs,", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"8341fca8-7b00-c948-ab95-1f48aadfd426"],

Cell["hysteresis differs,", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"374ab715-ebef-1049-a8ef-4e38af3c2878"],

Cell["transient stabilization differs.", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"bbeb7c2b-1e1a-6146-9e60-1bdba0822e45"],

Cell["This is very achievable. ", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"11905bb4-c7fb-4e4b-b22d-626efb0ddfa0"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["14.2. Breakthrough class B: measurement-state reporting", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"86860fce-08e0-0e4a-96f1-c7e7e584baa6"],

Cell["\<\
Augment experiments to report more than a scalar value. Add metadata streams \
for: \
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"900092ea-a131-4047-9fd7-56374c23eb63"],

Cell["effective coherence,", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"c21b9cf7-f177-5a4e-b5e4-97c9eebabb96"],

Cell["phase stability,", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"83442cfa-2d50-e149-822a-1140d670b0f3"],

Cell["hysteresis,", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"d1c165ea-b574-1840-b6ab-b71e8c89831a"],

Cell["thermal and geometric state,", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"f0396484-c3ab-4e4f-ac96-d83a382afc77"],

Cell["readout path dependence.", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"ce84276e-50af-af4c-85f0-269fdc820fc2"],

Cell["This is immediately implementable in many labs. ", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b3b84a1e-5bd6-4943-a82e-c326bdeb2e05"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["14.3. Breakthrough class C: multiscale probing", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"4f67ab48-e823-f143-b172-bb82ab347ef0"],

Cell["\<\
Instead of a single-resolution instrument, use nested-resolution probing and \
compare what stabilizes across scales.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"210ac111-b0d9-0a4b-b29e-51b0df5aad7b"],

Cell["This can be done in: ", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"71353969-1cc4-e849-a173-a4f469281173"],

Cell["microscopy,", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"d4612058-e132-b04d-b30d-4354d44b4995"],

Cell["resonator physics,", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"46dd4fbf-d9c3-6443-b669-af77c1f96d84"],

Cell["spectroscopy,", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"4853ccf5-a657-ee43-9fae-c67a3f8603b1"],

Cell["EM sensing,", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"5628d325-9546-bd46-a14a-d39b31afe9a2"],

Cell["material diagnostics.", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"813c9ef4-e0bf-6244-a650-42c0c975545f"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["14.4. Breakthrough class D: closure-sensitive resonators", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"41327205-c8a8-6d4d-84b9-90f8ba123896"],

Cell["\<\
Construct resonant systems with controllable recurrence structure and test \
whether persistent modes emerge that are not captured by naive scalar \
modeling.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"36d2d021-ad29-4c42-b1f7-6c922cb39952"],

Cell["This is realistic in RF, optics, and acoustics. ", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7c35687a-d064-9749-8160-0a61c4d8b90a"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["14.5. Breakthrough class E: biology-inspired sensors", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"02e63087-0b3e-9c46-82bb-e7abb3023dc6"],

Cell["\<\
Study why evolved sense organs use particular geometries and materials. \
Translate those into instrumentation principles.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"59ec840e-1570-004c-a15f-52909b54077e"],

Cell["\<\
This can produce actual engineering benefits regardless of whether the full \
ontology is correct. \
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3c55392e-644e-b844-86a9-30ed078451cc"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[GridBox[{
    {
     TemplateBox[{0},
      "Spacer1"]},
    {
